<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jandarids</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1292–1461</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Isfendiyarids</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jandarids, also called Isfendiyarids, were a Turkmen dynasty that ruled a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kastamonu">Kastamonu</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> port of Sinop from about 1292 to 1461. They long survived between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and other Anatolian powers, but the last ruler, Ismail Bey, surrendered Sinop to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a> in 1461, shortly before the Ottoman conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trabzon">Trebizond</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jandarids.jpg" alt="Jandarids" width="320" height="173" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: self- based on WP locator maps · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Candaro%C4%9Fullar%C4%B1.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
